    "description": "<SPAN style=\"FONT-SIZE: 7.5pt\"><?xml:namespace prefix = \"o\" ns = \"urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office\" /><o:p><SPAN lang=EN-GB>\n<P><FONT size=3>This poster was produced by a community group involved with the Wellington Unemployed Workers Union, and was printed with the help of the Wellington Media Collective.</FONT></P>\n<P><FONT size=3>Wellington Media Collective collaborated with the community to produce the poster as they were not trained artists. This was in line with WMC's philosophy: 'we will work with you, but not for you' (1979).</FONT></P>\n<P><FONT size=3>Working with the Collective meant that groups with very few resources could still produce powerful imagery and messaging, particularly those who were more likely to experience unemployment because of discrimination.</FONT></P></SPAN></o:p></SPAN>",
